@startuml ui_widgets
title UI Forms and Reusable Widgets

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #2B4C7E
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EEF5FF

package "Base widgets" {
  abstract class ITaskWidget <<QWidget>> {
    +loadConfigToTask()
    +loadConfigToWidget()
    #initPropertyBrowser(container)
    #changePropertyBrowserWidget(widget)
  }

  abstract class IDeviceWidget <<QWidget>> {
    +deviceId() : QString
    +loadConfigToDevice()
    +loadConfigToWidget()
    +getPropertyBrowser() : PropertyBrowserWidget*
  }

  class PropertyBrowserWidget <<QWidget>>
}

package "Task UI" {
  class LocalizationTaskWidget <<ITaskWidget>> {
    +loadConfigToTask()
    +loadConfigToWidget()
    -initNavPanel()
    -initContentStack()
    -rebuildDeviceNav()
    -getOrCreateDeviceConfigPage(deviceId) : QWidget*
  }

  class DeviceWidgetFactory {
    +createDeviceWidget(device, runner, dock, parent) : QWidget*
  }

  class LocalizationDashboardWidget <<ITaskWidget>> {
    -refreshTaskContext()
    -refreshTaskState()
    -refreshSignalMonitor()
    -updateCycleResult(result)
    -appendTaskLog(entry)
  }

  class LocalizationPatternsWidget <<ITaskWidget>> {
    -wireManagerSignals()
    -rebuildPatternTree()
    -onStartCommissionMatching()
  }

  class LocalizationSettingWidget <<ITaskWidget>> {
    -rebuildDeviceCombos()
    -rebuildCameraList()
    -rebuildCameraWorkspaceList()
    -onWorkspaceSetRequested(cameraId)
    -refreshCommTags(deviceId)
    -pushConfigToTask()
  }
}

package "Device config UI" {
  class BaslerCameraWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class JaiCameraWidget <<IDeviceWidget>> {
    -btn_trigger_clicked()
    -btn_auto_shot_clicked()
    -btn_backlight_toggle_clicked()
    -onContinuousFrameReady(result)
    -onContinuousStateChanged(active)
    -onBacklightStateChanged(on)
  }
  class JaiCamSelectDialog <<QDialog>>
  class MitsubishiMcDeviceWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class ModbusDeviceWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class VisionTcpipDeviceWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class VisionTcpipClientDeviceWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class VirtualDeviceWidget <<IDeviceWidget>>
  class VirtualPlcInputPanel
}
VirtualDeviceWidget ..> VirtualPlcInputPanel : only when the runner\nsupports input simulation
note bottom of VirtualPlcInputPanel
  Drives a hardware-free PLC's inputs so a project with
  no PLC on the network can run a cycle rather than stop
  at Ready. Every write goes through PlcRunner, never to
  the device.

  The one family-specific thing VirtualDeviceWidget does.
  It asks the RUNNER's capability, not the device's
  sub-type, so a device that would ignore the controls is
  never given them - and the generic widget still works
  for a fourth virtual family the day it is written.

  Commissioning shell only: ncr_runtime.exe has no device
  pages, and the operator shell is not a place to forge
  PLC inputs.
end note
note bottom of JaiCameraWidget
  A near-sibling of BaslerCameraWidget, deliberately: the
  device-info browser, connect/trigger controls and the
  whole calibration workflow exist twice. Unification is
  recorded debt, not an oversight.

  Its toggle buttons repaint from DEVICE-reported state,
  never from the last click - streaming and the backlight
  both change for reasons the widget did not cause.
end note
note bottom of ModbusDeviceWidget
  ONE widget serves both Modbus sub-types. The client and
  the server differ only in transport settings; the
  register-span editing and the live monitor are identical.
end note

